WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.397 --> 00:00:16.978
me! This is an order from the sultan!"

2
00:00:17.578 --> 00:00:19.259
shouted one of the sultan's men.

3
00:00:19.279 --> 00:00:23.020
"Cover your windows and close your doors.

4
00:00:24.421 --> 00:00:28.843
Princess Badra will pass through these streets today to go to the bathhouse.

5
00:00:30.343 --> 00:00:31.764
No one must look upon her!

6
00:00:32.972 --> 00:00:36.073
Whoever does not obey this order will be killed!"

7
00:00:38.635 --> 00:00:41.236
Did Aladdin run home when he heard these words?

8
00:00:41.956 --> 00:00:43.297
No, he did not.

9
00:00:43.317 --> 00:00:47.118
"Princess Badra," he sighed.

10
00:00:47.138 --> 00:00:50.560
"Everyone thinks she must be very lovely."

11
00:00:52.341 --> 00:00:53.021
It was true.

12
00:00:53.661 --> 00:00:55.542
She was very beautiful.

13
00:00:56.783 --> 00:00:59.364
But only a few people had ever seen her face.

14
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.864
Whenever Princess Badra left the palace, she always wore a veil.

15
00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:09.928
And every one of her visits to this bathhouse caused excitement.

16
00:01:09.948 --> 00:01:13.691
"Get off the street, you people!"

17
00:01:14.292 --> 00:01:16.113
yelled one man in a red cap.

18
00:01:17.415 --> 00:01:18.315
"Go home!"

19
00:01:18.896 --> 00:01:19.957
shouted an old woman.

20
00:01:19.977 --> 00:01:22.299
"Or hide in your shops!"

21
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.924
Aladdin stood in the street as the merchants and shoppers pushed past him.

22
00:01:29.768 --> 00:01:33.091
"I must see the face of the princess," Aladdin decided.

23
00:01:33.111 --> 00:01:37.775
"I've heard her eyes are deep and dark like the night sky."

24
00:01:38.916 --> 00:01:41.958
Soon Aladdin was the only one left in the street.

25
00:01:42.979 --> 00:01:46.402
Suddenly he heard the sound of flutes from around a corner.

26
00:01:46.422 --> 00:01:50.765
"It must be the princess and her attendants," said Aladdin.

27
00:01:50.785 --> 00:01:51.666
"I must hurry."

28
00:01:52.627 --> 00:01:55.829
He ran inside the bathhouse and quickly hid behind a door.

29
00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.612
He was just in time.

30
00:01:59.928 --> 00:02:04.491
Aladdin heard voices now, and one voice was sweeter than all the others.

31
00:02:04.511 --> 00:02:11.715
"How lovely it will be to relax in the hot steam," sighed the voice.

32
00:02:13.316 --> 00:02:17.878
As the princess entered the bathhouse, Aladdin peeked out from behind the door.

33
00:02:19.099 --> 00:02:22.841
Just then Princess Badra removed the veil from her face.

34
00:02:22.861 --> 00:02:26.643
"Oh my!"

35
00:02:27.003 --> 00:02:27.884
whispered Aladdin.

36
00:02:29.316 --> 00:02:34.100
Aladdin saw her deep, dark eyes and her smiling, red mouth.

37
00:02:35.481 --> 00:02:36.501
He could not breathe.

38
00:02:37.262 --> 00:02:38.262
He could not move!

39
00:02:38.282 --> 00:02:45.728
"I know nothing of beauty," he thought, "but I know Princess Badra must be the most beautiful girl

40
00:02:45.768 --> 00:02:46.488
in the world."

41
00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:52.092
In one moment, he had fallen in love with the sultan's daughter.

42
00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:57.176
No one saw Aladdin as he left the bathhouse through a back door.

43
00:02:59.948 --> 00:03:04.010
When he returned home, his mother said, "Back so soon?"

44
00:03:06.271 --> 00:03:07.491
Aladdin did not answer.

45
00:03:08.151 --> 00:03:11.072
He sat down on a cushion and stared into space.

46
00:03:11.092 --> 00:03:14.854
"Eat something," Zeba said.

47
00:03:16.074 --> 00:03:18.475
She set some bread and dried fruits before him.

48
00:03:18.495 --> 00:03:20.216
"You don't look well."

49
00:03:21.977 --> 00:03:27.099
She poured him a cup of strong coffee, but Aladdin still did not say a word.

50
00:03:27.119 --> 00:03:29.600
"What has happened to you?"

51
00:03:30.224 --> 00:03:30.764
she asked.

52
00:03:30.784 --> 00:03:33.226
"Why won't you speak to me?"

53
00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:38.749
"Please, leave me alone," Aladdin answered.

54
00:03:40.109 --> 00:03:42.631
He ate a bite of bread and then went to his room.

55
00:03:43.431 --> 00:03:45.492
He lay awake all night.

56
00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:49.835
Morning came, but Aladdin still did not move.

57
00:03:51.215 --> 00:03:52.236
Zeba was worried.

58
00:03:52.256 --> 00:03:53.957
"Are you in pain?"

59
00:03:54.657 --> 00:03:55.118
she said.

60
00:03:55.138 --> 00:03:56.738
"Shall I get a doctor?"

61
00:03:56.758 --> 00:04:00.329
"I am not sick," he murmured.

62
00:04:00.349 --> 00:04:01.750
"I am in love."

63
00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:03.851
"In love!"

64
00:04:04.552 --> 00:04:05.993
cried his mother with delight.

65
00:04:06.013 --> 00:04:08.295
"Oh, my son!

66
00:04:08.855 --> 00:04:10.136
Who is this lucky lady?

67
00:04:10.637 --> 00:04:11.437
Tell me quickly!"

68
00:04:11.458 --> 00:04:17.302
"I am in love with Princess Badra," said Aladdin calmly.

69
00:04:17.322 --> 00:04:20.024
"And I have decided to marry her."

70
00:04:21.045 --> 00:04:25.929
Aladdin's mother stared at him with surprise and then burst out laughing.

71
00:04:30.549 --> 00:04:32.450
"Marry the sultan's daughter?

72
00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:35.333
You? A tailor's son?"

73
00:04:35.353 --> 00:04:39.837
"Yes," said Aladdin quietly.

74
00:04:39.857 --> 00:04:41.598
"I will marry her."

75
00:04:42.939 --> 00:04:49.885
Zeba raised her hands over her head and cried out, "My son has lost his mind!

76
00:04:50.546 --> 00:04:52.868
The genies have made him crazy!"
